  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cdc7e29e-d309-453d-b111-7d63e8f169fe",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Normalización y organización\n",
    "\n",
    "Aplana la matriz y normaliza los valores de los píxeles, teniendo en cuenta que cada uno de los canales RGB contienen numeros enteros que varían entre 0 y 255."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "87397865-8ba2-4dbd-af8e-af3581db4592",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Dim1: 500\n",
      "Dim2: 1109\n",
      "Dim3: 3\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "dim1 = image_array.shape[0]\n",
    "dim2 = image_array.shape[1]\n",
    "dim3 = image_array.shape[2]\n",
    "print(f'Dim1: {dim1}\\nDim2: {dim2}\\nDim3: {dim3}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "980011f5-7047-4990-930a-ea996d6846db",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pixels = np.reshape(image_array, (dim1, dim2*dim3))/255.0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9c93db8d-a28e-4a87-b136-7c4ec15420e7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# PCA\n",
    "\n",
    "Se crea una instancia con el número de componentes que se desean."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "2d3c006b-2f45-4151-a3aa-16abd6cec9f5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pca_5 = PCA(n_components=5)\n",
    "pca_25 = PCA(n_components=25)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "ccac95ea-ce34-4704-b423-f80066bed971",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdin",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Indique el número de componentes que desea: 15\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "n_componentes = int(input('Indique el número de componentes que desea:'))\n",
    "pca_n = PCA(n_components=n_componentes)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7e989392-4e0e-4861-b588-1769df968a7e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Ajuste\n",
    "\n",
    "Se realiza el ajuste a los datos de los pixeles normalizados"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "d54e3d5f-cbf7-4496-b369-98c233556a0c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pca_5.fit(pixels)\n",
    "pixels_pca_5 = pca_5.transform(pixels)\n",
    "\n",
    "pca_25.fit(pixels)\n",
    "pixels_pca_25 = pca_25.transform(pixels)\n",
    "\n",
    "pca_n.fit(pixels)\n",
    "pixels_pca_n = pca_n.transform(pixels)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "id": "adc03e98-182b-4da2-9942-a221e84418e5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Con 5 componentes los resultados son:\n",
      "Las dimensiones quedan cómo: (500, 5)\n",
      "\n",
      "La varianza explicada por cada una de las componentes principales es: [0.38325922 0.09739478 0.06897662 0.0514409  0.02889081]\n",
      "\n",
      "La varianza total explicada por las componentes es: 0.6299623281621345\n",
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print('Con 5 componentes los resultados son:')\n",
    "print('Las dimensiones quedan cómo:', pixels_pca_5.shape, end='\\n\\n')\n",
    "\n",
    "print('La varianza explicada por cada una de las componentes principales es:', pca_5.explained_variance_ratio_, end='\\n\\n')\n",
    "\n",
    "print('La varianza total explicada por las componentes es:', np.sum(pca_5.explained_variance_ratio_), end='\\n\\n')"
   ]
  },
  {
